# T-009 — active indent guide (F19) and graceful --quit (F18)

Completed 2026-10-18. PASS. No git, network, shared STATUS.md edits, or process termination. All edits/build/selftest artifacts stay in src/AntiQuickPad/ and the authorized T-009 report/status/PNG paths.

## Implementation

- `Look.IndentGuideActive` is #71859B versus normal #445160; both use the existing 1 DIP thickness. On the editor background #171D25, the active RGB distance from the background is exactly 2x normal. The caret selects the deepest completed four-column indent on its line. Only that column brightens across the contiguous block at that depth, stopping on a dedent, fence delimiter, or code/text transition. Blank continuation uses the existing guide-depth rule. Fence body indentation is read from the body, not the delimiter. Unindented caret lines have no active guide.
- Caret PositionChanged updates the renderer's caret line and calls `InvalidateLayer(KnownLayer.Background)` only; this handler does not request layout or regenerate visual lines.
- `--quit` returns before constructing Avalonia or acquiring residency. It opens the existing per-user/session singleton objects, signals the added Quit event, and uses the resident PID published in a named mapping to wait for actual process exit within a shared 5-second budget. No resident returns 0 immediately. Timeout returns 1 with `AntiQuickPad --quit: resident did not exit within 5 seconds.` Normal second-launch Show signalling is unchanged.
- Resident command quit dispatches to the same save/close/shutdown method as tray Quit. Start and finish logs include `source=command`. If saving fails, the command path logs the failure and keeps the resident alive without showing its window; the client eventually times out. Tray save-failure visibility remains intact.

## Pixel proof

[T-009-active.png](T-009-active.png), **1596 x 510 pixels**, two actual 798 x 510 editor captures at 96 DPI / scale 1, side by side. Left: caret in nested list item. Right: caret in Python body. Opened and visually inspected the final PNG: the correct guide is brighter in each pane, the other guides remain subtle, and the caret is visible at the respective text end.

Measurements compare caret-hidden active captures against an otherwise identical unindented-caret baseline; visible-caret captures are used in the delivered image.

| Caret | Active column / pixel X | Block lines | Brighter pixels | Changed pixels elsewhere |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Nested list, line 3 | column 8 / x=122 | 3–5 | 70 | 0 |
| Python body, line 11 | column 8 / x=122 | 11–12 | 46 | 0 |

Sample guide RGB changes **(68,81,96) -> (113,133,155)** in both fixtures. Every changed guide pixel increases all RGB channels. All other guide columns, text and pixels outside the selected block remain byte-identical. Moving the caret to unindented line 15 restores the baseline byte-for-byte.

Existing checkbox, passive-guide and strike proofs also pass and write only authorized names: T-009-checkbox.png, T-009-guides.png, T-009-strike.png.

## Verification

Commands from src/AntiQuickPad:

```powershell
$env:AVALONIA_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT='1'
dotnet build -c Release --no-restore -p:UseSharedCompilation=false
dotnet bin/Release/net10.0/AntiQuickPad.dll --selftest
```

Final Release build: **exit 0, 0 warnings, 0 errors**, 2.17 seconds. Normal bin/Release was available; no fallback output path was used.

Full selftest: **exit 0**. Added checks:

- Isolated-name actual resident process receives command quit, saves a pending editor change, logs command start/finish, and exits 0 before the command returns 0. Fixture startup plus quit: **1157 ms**. No second-launch Show log.
- Quit after that resident has exited: **exit 0**, with no resident started.
- Isolated deliberately unresponsive resident: command returns **exit 1 after 5091 ms** (including child process startup), with the expected timeout message verified from stderr. The fixture exits itself normally after 7 seconds; no process was killed.
- Save failure: command quit keeps hidden resident alive; ordinary Quit still restores visible error status. Existing successful quit start/finish, editor, persistence/reload, carousel, focus and second-launch checks pass.

Internal scripted show-to-focus: **2.367 / 1.615 / 1.589 ms**; not physical hotkey-to-paint measurements.

## User-facing checks still needed

1. Launch this new Release build. Move the caret among nested list and Python indentation levels, then an unindented line; check active contrast and block extent at your usual Windows DPI.
2. Check scrolling, wrapping and folded content in real notes, including indented fences and tabs.
3. Edit a note, hide the pad, then run `src/AntiQuickPad/bin/Release/net10.0/AntiQuickPad.exe --quit`; confirm it stays hidden, the tray icon disappears, and the edit survives relaunch. Run again with no resident and confirm exit 0.
4. Check tray Quit and ordinary second launch still behave as expected with the new build. An older resident must be relaunched once into this build to understand the new Quit signal.

The isolated scripted resident and rendered fixtures passed. Physical interaction and mixed-DPI behavior were not manually tested.

